instruction:
How can I randomly generate a two-letter word with a score of at least 10 using valid Scrabble words in Latex? Given the following list of Scrabble words with their corresponding scores:
\begin{table}[h]
\centering
\begin{tabular}{|c|c|}
\hline
\textbf{Word} & \textbf{Score} \\ \hline
aa & 1 \\ \hline
ab & 2 \\ \hline
ad & 1 \\ \hline
ae & 1 \\ \hline
... & ... \\ \hline
\end{tabular}
\end{table}
I can use the following Latex code to randomly select a two-letter word with a score of 10 or higher:
\begin{lstlisting}[language=TeX]
\usepackage{pgf,pgffor}
\def\scrabblewords{aa/1, ab/2, ad/1, ae/1, ...}
\def\validwords{}
\foreach \word/\score in \scrabblewords {
  \ifnum\score>9
    \xdef\validwords{\validwords,\word}
  \fi
}
\edef\randomword{\noexpand\pgfmathrandomitem{\noexpand\w}{\validwords}\noexpand\w}
\randomword
\end{lstlisting} 
Is there a better way to achieve this?

