Swift does not have a built-in library or function specifically designed to detect and correct homophone errors in text. However, there are third-party libraries and APIs that can be used to accomplish this task.
One popular option is the LanguageTool API, which is a free and open-source grammar and style checker that supports multiple languages, including English. You can use the API to check for homophones and other grammar errors in your text and receive suggestions for corrections.
To use the LanguageTool API in Swift, you can make HTTP requests to the API endpoint and parse the JSON response to extract the suggested corrections. Here's an example code snippet:
```
let text = "He red the book too quickly and missed important details."
let url = URL(string: "https://languagetool.org/api/v2/check?text=\(text)&language=en-US")!
let task = URLSession.shared.dataTask(with: url) { data, response, error in
    guard let data = data else {
        print("Error: \(error?.localizedDescription ?? "Unknown error")")
        return
    }

    do {
        let json = try JSONSerialization.jsonObject(with: data, options: []) as! [String: Any]
        let matches = json["matches"] as! [[String: Any]]

        for match in matches {
            let message = match["message"] as! String
            let replacements = match["replacements"] as! [[String: Any]]

            if message.contains("Did you mean") {
                let suggestion = replacements[0]["value"] as! String
                let startIndex = text.index(text.startIndex, offsetBy: match["offset"] as! Int)
                let endIndex = text.index(startIndex, offsetBy: match["length"] as! Int)
                let range = startIndex..<endIndex

                let correctedText = text.replacingCharacters(in: range, with: suggestion)
                print("Original text: \(text)")
                print("Corrected text: \(correctedText)")
            }
        }
    } catch {
        print("Error parsing JSON: \(error.localizedDescription)")
    }
}
task.resume()
```
This code sends a GET request to the LanguageTool API with the text to be checked as a query parameter. The API responds with a JSON object containing information about any grammar errors found in the text. The code then extracts the suggested replacements for any homophone errors and replaces the incorrect word with the suggested correction.
Note that the LanguageTool API has a rate limit of 20 requests per minute for the free version, so you may need to implement some throttling logic to avoid exceeding this limit.

