```
In this example, we allocate memory for the input data using a function called `allocate_memory()`, which ensures that we only allocate the amount of memory that we need. After running inference, we free up the memory used by the input and output data using a function called `free_memory()`. By managing memory in this way, we can ensure that we are not wasting resources on unnecessary memory allocation, which can improve the performance of our machine learning algorithm on a low-power device like a Raspberry Pi.

