To customize the message for each user based on their IP address, you can use a GeoIP database to determine the user's location based on their IP address. Here's a sample code in C# that demonstrates how to achieve this using basic programming techniques:
```
using System.Net;
using System.IO;
public static string GetUserLocation(string ipAddress)
{
    string url = "http://ip-api.com/json/" + ipAddress;
    string response = "";
    try
    {
        HttpWebRequest request = (HttpWebRequest)WebRequest.Create(url);
        request.Method = "GET";
        using (HttpWebResponse webResponse = (HttpWebResponse)request.GetResponse())
        {
            using (Stream stream = webResponse.GetResponseStream())
            {
                StreamReader reader = new StreamReader(stream, System.Text.Encoding.UTF8);
                response = reader.ReadToEnd();
            }
        }
    }
    catch (Exception ex)
    {
        response = "";
    }
    return response;
}
```
This code sends a GET request to the IP-API website and retrieves the user's location based on their IP address. You can then parse the response JSON to extract the user's region and display a personalized message based on their location.
Note that this solution relies on a third-party GeoIP database and may not be accurate in all cases. It also assumes that you have a way to map each user's IP address to their session on your web page.

