What is the best way to parse JSON data retrieved from an API using Swift? Can you provide a code snippet that includes a function to parse the JSON and populate a custom data model? 
Here's an example JSON data:
```swift
[
    {
        "id": 1,
        "title": "Post 1",
        "body": "Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit."
    },
    {
        "id": 2,
        "title": "Post 2",
        "body": "Nulla eget sapien ac mi bibendum blandit non non nibh."
    }
]
```
And here's a code snippet that you can use to parse this data and populate a custom data model:
```swift
struct Post: Codable {
    let id: Int
    let title: String
    let body: String
}
func fetchData() {
    let urlString = "https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts"
    let url = URL(string: urlString)!
    let task = URLSession.shared.dataTask(with: url) { data, response, error in
        guard let data = data, error == nil else {
            print(error?.localizedDescription ?? "Unknown error")
            return
        }

        do {
            let posts = try JSONDecoder().decode([Post].self, from: data)
            print(posts)
        } catch {
            print(error.localizedDescription)
        }
    }

    task.resume()
}
fetchData()
```
This code uses the `Codable` protocol to define a custom data model called `Post`. It then defines a function called `fetchData()` that retrieves JSON data from an API and uses the `JSONDecoder` class to decode the data into an array of `Post` objects. The `print()` statement in the `do` block then displays the parsed data in the console.

